    <string name="about">About</string>
    <string name="about_what">What it does</string>
    <string name="about_what_text">NexScreen changes the screen density (DPI) and resolution globally or per app, with or without root.</string>
    <string name="about_how">How it works</string>
    <string name="about_how_text">It runs the wm density and wm size system commands using Shizuku or ADB if you don\'t have root, and with root (su) if you do; pick whichever you prefer from the start of the app. Changes are temporary: confirm them from the dialog that appears or they revert on their own, and per-app profiles are restored when you leave that app.</string>
    <string name="about_games">Games</string>
    <string name="about_games_text">Screen changes are temporary: they apply only while the app is in the foreground and revert when you leave. This app doesn\'t use overlays, accessibility, Xposed or read other processes\' memory, so it injects nothing into games and shouldn\'t affect titles like Free Fire.</string>
    <string name="about_permissions">Permissions</string>
    <string name="about_permissions_text">• Shizuku: run system commands.\n• Usage access: know which app is in the foreground.</string>
    <string name="about_credits">Credits</string>
    <string name="about_credits_text">Developer: Nexun\n\nLibraries:\n• Shizuku — Rikka Apps\n• Jetpack Compose and Material 3 — Google\n• Kotlin — JetBrains\n\n%1$s</string>
